Ticket **#4471** was marked known as a single month-flip parser bug. The merged reports
are **412** unique ids. The cause logic in `#lib/kb/causes` splits them into two problems
that need their own tickets.

<Callout kind="warn">
Subject-line dedupe (decision 0001) merged two different bugs into one ticket. Split them.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

1. **parser** — day-first tenants; the shared parser reads every date month first. Dates
   flip. Covers the reports whose channel is not a `booking-v3` form with an `MM/…` hint.
2. **hint** — day-first tenants on `booking-v3`; the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the
   field, people type month first, and the form still reads the tenant's day-first way.
   A different bug from the shared parser.

File one engineering ticket per cause. Do not keep both under #4471.

